[Cross-session delivery notice] Your message to another session was held by that session (recipient: uds:/tmp/cc-socks/65373.sock; msg_id: de492f65-357e-4dfe-8a96-1f701d5e948c). NOT delivered: its Claude has not seen it. Don't report it as delivered, don't wait for a reply, and don't resend while it's held. The usual cause is that the two sessions run in different permission modes: a terminal session asks its user to approve, but a Claude Desktop or non-interactive session can't ask, so the hold expires undelivered unless the modes match. A session can also be set to hold every message. Another notice follows on release, denial, or expiry. Tell your user what's held and why, or pick another approach.
